_refine_special_details          
; 
 Refinement of F^2^ against ALL reflections.  The weighted R-factor wR and 
 goodness of fit S are based on F^2^, conventional R-factors R are based 
 on F, with F set to zero for negative F^2^. The threshold expression of 
 F^2^ > 2sigma(F^2^) is used only for calculating R-factors(gt) etc. and is 
 not relevant to the choice of reflections for refinement.  R-factors based 
 on F^2^ are statistically about twice as large as those based on F, and R- 
 factors based on ALL data will be even larger. 
The asymmetric unit contains a Dy ion, half a Dy ion and half a Cr ion, with two chloride counter-ions and two fully and one partially occupied water solvent molecule. The large spurious residual peak is found 0.8 A away from the Dy ion.
All non-H atoms were refined anisotrpically and all H-atoms were placed in calculated positions, except for the H-atoms of the H2O molecules and two of the H-atoms of a isonicotinate ligand, which could not be found or calculated. The H-atoms for the hydroxide ligands were found with a theraml parameter set at 1.2 x that od the adjacent O atom. Thermal (ISOR) and bond (DFIX) restraints where placed on several atoms.  

;

